---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteScripts from '../components/SiteScripts.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../data/site';
import { LOGO_PATH } from '../data/brand';

const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'feedback@plozz.app';
const SENTRY_PRIVACY_URL = 'https://sentry.io/privacy/';
const GITHUB_PRIVACY_URL = 'https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement';
const LAST_UPDATED = 'October 26, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Plozz"
  description="What Plozz shares, why, and how you control it. Plain-language information about optional diagnostics, connected services and iCloud."
>
  <main class="legal">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="legal-home" href="/">
        <img src={LOGO_PATH} alt="" width="28" height="28" />
        <span>Plozz</span>
      </a>

      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <p>
        Plozz plays media from sources you choose. There’s no Plozz account
        or usage analytics. You decide whether to share diagnostics.
      </p>

      <h2>Open source</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href={GITHUB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">app code</a> and{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/brandomoore/plozz-website" target="_blank" rel="noopener">website code</a>{' '}
        are public. You can inspect how Plozz handles data and connects to
        services. This doesn’t make your media or private reports public.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional diagnostics</h2>
      <p>
        Current builds ask you to choose{' '}
        <strong>Share Diagnostics</strong> or <strong>Don’t Share</strong>.
        Either choice lets you use the app. Sharing stays off until you agree.
        You can change this device’s choice in Help &amp; Diagnostics.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reports can include errors, app and device details, performance
        measurements and which part of the app was open. Plozz filters account
        details, network request information and raw activity messages from
        automatic reports before sending them.
      </p>
      <p>
        With sharing enabled, <strong>“Send to Developer”</strong> sends filtered
        technical details and an optional message only when you press it.
        These reports use fresh labels instead of saved account or media
        identifiers. Your message stays attached to the report and is sent
        as written. Don’t include passwords or other information you don’t
        want to share.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={SENTRY_PRIVACY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sentry</a>{' '}
        processes and stores reports for us on servers in the United States.
        We use diagnostics and support reports only to investigate problems,
        fix bugs and improve Plozz—not for advertising, marketing, profiling
        users or selling their data. Filtering doesn’t guarantee anonymity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Turning sharing off stops future automatic reports and disables
        “Send to Developer”. It doesn’t delete reports already sent.
      </p>
      <p id="build-differences">
        <strong>Older beta builds</strong> may have different sharing defaults
        and send raw logs containing server addresses, account or media IDs,
        titles and search text. Check your settings and review the activity
        shown before sending a report.
      </p>

      <h2>Feedback and support</h2>
      <p>
        “Report a Problem” opens a pre-filled{' '}
        <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub issue</a>{' '}
        with app, device and recent technical activity details. Review it
        before posting. Your post and GitHub identity are public, under{' '}
        <a href={GITHUB_PRIVACY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub’s privacy policy</a>.
        For private feedback, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your servers and connected services</h2>
      <p>
        Media-server logins are kept in Apple’s Keychain. Connecting to your
        server doesn’t send those logins to us. Plozz profiles don’t replace
        your server’s account permissions or watch history.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your servers and the services used for artwork, metadata and subtitles
        receive the requests needed for those features, including your IP
        address. Some connections, including Plex and Jellyfin-compatible
        servers, also use a saved device identifier.
      </p>
      <p>
        Optional services such as Trakt, AniList, MyAnimeList, Simkl, Last.fm,
        WeTrakr and Seerr receive the watchlist, playback or request activity
        you enable. Their own privacy policies apply; they may retain
        account-linked data for purposes such as recommendations or analytics.
        This isn’t a Plozz-operated analytics service.
      </p>

      <h2>iCloud and other devices</h2>
      <p>
        Optional iCloud Sync keeps profiles, settings, server details,
        watchlists and supported Live TV setup in your private iCloud
        storage. Supported tracker and Live TV credentials use encrypted
        storage. Movies and offline downloads aren’t synced.
      </p>
      <p>
        On iPhone and iPad, supported server logins can also sync through
        iCloud Keychain. Apple TV doesn’t use that path. Supported tracker
        logins can use iCloud Keychain independently of Plozz’s iCloud Sync
        setting. You can also approve transferring eligible logins between
        devices; Silo must pair again. See{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.plozz.app/profiles-and-sync/">Profiles and sync</a>{' '}
        for controls and provider limits.
      </p>

      <h2>Connecting accounts</h2>
      <p>
        To connect AniList or MyAnimeList, our website briefly holds an
        authorization token while passing it to your device. It’s deleted
        after use and configured to expire after ten minutes.
      </p>
      <p>
        PublicMetaDB browser pairing encrypts your key before sending it to
        the pairing service. The encrypted handoff is removed after
        completion or cancellation; pairing data expires after ten minutes.
      </p>
      <p>
        These connection helpers temporarily count requests by IP address
        to prevent code guessing and abuse. Those counts are also
        configured to expire after ten minutes.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare</a>{' '}
        hosts this website, which also requests our public GitHub star count.
        These providers handle connection data and infrastructure logs under
        their own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Plozz is a general-purpose player. Parents and guardians should choose
        suitable sources and review diagnostics-sharing choices. See{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.plozz.app/parental-controls/">Parental controls</a>{' '}
        for setup and limits.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact and changes</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or requests, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        Policy updates will appear here with a revised date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
  <SiteScripts />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 64px 0 88px;
  }

  .legal .container {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .legal-home {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    font-weight: var(--w-strong);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    transition: color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .legal-home:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .legal-home img {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    image-rendering: pixelated;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-top: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--brand);
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
